---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import Base from "../layouts/base.astro";
import NormalBlock from "../components/normal_block.astro";
import Note from "../components/note.astro";
import Certificates from "../components/certificates.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/page_header.astro";

import aniko from "../assets/images/photos/aniko.jpg";
import podcast from "../assets/images/photos/podcast.jpg";
import aniko4 from "../assets/images/photos/aniko-4.jpg";

const metadata = {
    title: "Colour consultant, coach, and colour interpreter",
    description: "Discover my story and methods! Colour interpretation, coaching, and colour consultancy with international experience.",
    type: "website",
};
---

<Base metadata={metadata}>
    <PageHeader title="About me" />
    <NormalBlock title="Who am I?">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-8 items-center">
            <div>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">I am a wife, mother, Personal Stylist and Colour Consultant, passionate about helping
                    women discover themselves through colour, fashion and personal style.</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">From 2016 until August 2026, I lived in England with my family, first in Southampton,
                    before we began a new chapter in Glasgow, Scotland. Living in the UK introduced me to different cultures,
                    broadened my perspective and helped me grow both personally and professionally.</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">Since childhood, I have felt drawn to supporting people and understanding the feelings
                    and thoughts that lie beneath the surface. Growing up with a mother who struggled with bipolar disorder
                    taught me early on about the importance of self-awareness, emotional resilience and nurturing our inner
                    resources. Alongside this, I have always loved fashion and colour, gradually discovering how beautifully
                    these passions connect with self-expression and personal growth.</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">In 2020, I immersed myself in the world of colour psychology and the deeper emotional
                    meanings colours can hold for each of us. I became fascinated by how our personal connection with colour
                    goes far beyond fashion, influencing our emotions, self-expression and the way we experience the world
                    around us. And that's how I fell in love with the world of colour, a passion that continues to inspire
                    me every day.</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">To deepen my knowledge, I studied at the London College of Style (LCS), completing
                    the Colour Analysis course and later the Personal Style course. These experiences allowed me to bring
                    together my love of colour, fashion and self-expression, and explore how our appearance can reflect our
                    individuality and support our confidence.</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">For me, personal style has never been just about clothes. It is about discovering
                    who we are, expressing our individuality and finding the confidence to be ourselves.</p>
            </div>
            <Image class="min-h-full md:max-h-[700px] xl:max-h-[560px] object-cover justify-self-center pb-4" src={aniko4} alt="" />
        </div>
        <Certificates />
    </NormalBlock>
    <NormalBlock title="Creativity, Fashion and My Instagram Journey">
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">One of the most valuable experiences in my journey was volunteering as a window dresser at
            the British Heart Foundation in Southampton for around a year and a half. This experience allowed me to develop
            my creativity, experiment with colour combinations and explore a wide range of fashion and personal styles,
            including those very different from my own taste. I learned to appreciate different styles objectively and create
            eye-catching window displays that reflected the seasons and the shop's ever-changing selection.</p>
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">During this time, I also started my Instagram account, initially sharing outfit inspiration
            created using pieces available in the charity shop, including items featured in my window displays. Today,
            Instagram remains an important creative space for me, where I share colourful outfit ideas every day, often
            presented through my own artistic perspective.</p>
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">
            I believe that different colour combinations and styling ideas can inspire others to experiment, discover their
            own style and express themselves more confidently. I am incredibly grateful for the kind and encouraging feedback
            I have received so far.</p>
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">Alongside fashion, I also enjoy sharing everyday experiences and more personal, emotional
            topics that I believe many people can relate to. Being able to connect with others through both creativity and
            honest conversations means a great deal to me. I want my content to be about more than beautiful outfits; I want
            it to inspire, encourage and remind people that there is always room for individuality, colour and self-expression
            in everyday life.</p>

